              "evidenceCode": "ECO:0000269",
              "source": "PubMed",
              "id": "31950558"
            }
          ],
          "value": "Catalyzes the reversible phosphorylation of S-methyl-5'-thioadenosine (MTA) to adenine and 5-methylthioribose-1-phosphate (PubMed:23042035, PubMed:31950558). Involved in the breakdown of MTA, a major by-product of polyamine biosynthesis. Responsible for the first step in the methionine salvage pathway after MTA has been generated from S-adenosylmethionine. Has broad substrate specificity with 6-aminopurine nucleosides as preferred substrates (By similarity). Also catalyzes the phosphorylation of 5'-deoxyadenosine (5'dAdo) to 5-deoxyribose 1-phosphate (PubMed:31950558). Part of a bifunctional DHAP-shunt salvage pathway for SAM by-products (PubMed:31950558)"
        }
      ],
      "commentType": "FUNCTION"
